# Version

There is one number, in the `VERSION` file at the root. `package.json` and the image do not repeat it. While the mode is observation, major stays 0.

- Closed work raises only the patch. It was `0.1.1`, it became `0.1.2`. `CHANGELOG.md` gets a paragraph of what went in. The tag `v0.1.2` sits on the commit that closes it.
- Do not raise the minor. A person changes it by hand and says so separately. Do not set the minor yourself, even when the work is large.
- A breaking `/v1` contract or a product boundary raises the major and starts a new path prefix. Ordinary work does not change `/v1` and does not open `/v2`. Do not set the major until a person has asked for it.
- A commit on main does not move the number by itself. Several commits of one change wait for one tag.
- Unclosed work is written under `Unreleased` and is not part of the number.
- Commit messages are English.
- The customer agent carries the same number. `ledgesec-agent` embeds `VERSION` at build time, and the installed Lua module reads a copy of that file. Do not copy the number into `Cargo.toml`. A batch names the build with the `agent` field. The cabinet shows the number that arrived with the host.
